+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to format a value as multiple parts, largest unit first. The output is compatible with Go's [`time.ParseDuration`](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration): parts are glued together without spaces and hours are the largest unit (no days).
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })        // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })       // "25h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })       // "-1h30m"
+ms(1999, { compound: true })           // "1s"
+ms(999, { compound: true })            // "0s"
+```
+
+Zero parts are skipped and leftover milliseconds are dropped, so values under one second return `"0s"`. Compound only applies to the short format: if `long: true` is also set, `long` wins.
+
